      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The skepticism persists because the definition of \"implementation\" is extremely broad, and many initial efforts lack rigorous, longitudinal measurement against direct financial metrics. Critics accurately point out that poorly managed mandates can indeed introduce friction or undermine established merit-based systems. Therefore, the debate isn't settled; it shifts from *if* it works to *how* to measure the specific, nuanced ROI while mitigating valid cultural risks.",
      "source": "target",
